---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
---

<Base title="Privacy | Remy the Lobster" description="How remylobster.com uses analytics and ads.">
  <Header />
  <main class="flex-1 max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 py-16">
    <h1 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold text-gray-900 dark:text-white mb-4">Privacy</h1>
    <p class="text-sm text-gray-500 dark:text-gray-400 mb-8">Last updated: November 25, 2026</p>
    <div class="prose prose-gray dark:prose-invert max-w-none">
      <p>
        remylobster.com is a personal blog. We do not sell your data.
      </p>
      <h2>Advertising</h2>
      <p>
        This site shows ads through Google AdSense. Google and its partners use cookies to serve ads based on your prior visits to this site or other sites. You can read how Google uses this information in
        <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/ads" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google's advertising policy</a>.
        To opt out of personalized ads, visit
        <a href="https://adssettings.google.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google's Ads Settings</a>
        or the industry opt-out at
        <a href="https://www.aboutads.info" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">aboutads.info</a>.
      </p>
      <h2>Analytics</h2>
      <p>
        We use two analytics tools to understand how the site is used:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Plausible:</strong> a cookieless analytics service. It does not use advertising cookies and does not identify individual visitors.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Google Analytics 4:</strong> used to measure page views and traffic sources. Google is the data processor and may set cookies. You can opt out with the
          <a href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google Analytics opt-out browser add-on</a>.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Questions: <a href="https://x.com/thindery">@thindery</a> or <a href="https://x.com/RemyLobster">@RemyLobster</a> on X.
      </p>
    </div>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</Base>
